  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The specification uses the task-level search_object, approach_object, search_zone, and approach_zone actions; color observations; claim actions and received-claim observations; pickup and drop actions with their outcomes; and delivery publication actions. Low-level movement and obstacle events are omitted because collision_avoidance already protects motion, while release and peer-delivery events are not required to sequence one robot's own collection and matching-zone delivery.",
    "transition_design": "object_search selects one unified red, green, or blue branch only after the corresponding object-visible observation. Each claim-attempt state permits only its matching claim and abandons the attempt on the matching received-claim or not-visible observation. A claim immediately enters an object-approach state with repeatable approach_object; loss observations return to repeatable search_object states. pick_up_object is enabled only after the matching object-reached observation. Confirmed pickup starts matching-zone search, approach_zone is enabled only after matching-zone visibility, and drop_object is enabled only after the matching zone-reached observation. Pickup and delivery failures return to retry phases, confirmed delivery requires the matching publication event, and only delivery_complete is marked. No cross-color drop path or low-level motion decision is introduced.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
  }
